TASK
Research AliExpress candidates for {{category_and_use_case}}.
Target landed-price budget and currency: {{budget}}
Required sizes, composition and features: {{sizes_and_materials}}
Delivery destination and deadline, if any: {{destination}}
Requested number of candidates: {{candidate_limit}}
Existing supplier records to reuse: {{existing_supplier_list}}

Use current accessible listing pages, seller pages and customer-feedback details. Set the actual destination and exact variant before comparing price, delivery or availability. If live browsing is unavailable, return a research worksheet with missing fields; do not fabricate a shortlist. Use permitted browsing or authorized platform tools and do not bypass access controls. Deduplicate the same item/store pair and identify apparent duplicate listings across stores without assuming the manufacturer is the same.

For each candidate record: item ID and URL; store name/ID/URL; selected variant; material/size chart evidence; observed rating; rating count; written-review count if different; displayed sold figure with its original wording and known time/variant scope; recent-review sample and date range; repeated fit, quality or delivery themes; selected-variant price; shipping and visible tax; estimated landed cost; delivery estimate; current returns eligibility and its source; stock state; access date. Unknown values remain null. A rounded '1,000+' sold figure is a lower bound, not an exact count. Listing-wide ratings are not variant-specific proof.

Apply Wow Fashion sourcing rubric v1: adjusted rating 30 points, sold-volume signal 15, recent-review evidence 15, seller evidence 15, fit/specification clarity 10, comparable landed value 10 and delivery/returns clarity 5. Use the formula and anchored grades in the portal; do not invent manual grades without reasons. Show evidence completeness separately and never rescale an incomplete score to 100. Sales alone do not prove quality; a high star average with very few reviews should not automatically outrank a well-evidenced product.

Flag hard failures and unresolved identity, material, sizing, authenticity or destination issues before ranking. Propose up to five candidates with evidence-based reasons, tradeoffs and the next verification step. Strong scores create a shortlist for human/sample review, not an approved supplier or a claim that the item has been tested. Extract supplier leads as unverified records, with no invented manufacturer details.

