TASK
Research this supplier lead:
Store or business URL: {{store_url}}
Relevant product listings: {{candidate_products}}
Available business evidence: {{business_documents}}
Documented contact history: {{contact_history}}
Sample-order records: {{sample_results}}

Record the exact trading name, platform store ID, store URL, public business name and location where published, observed store age and feedback with timestamps, category focus, associated product IDs and public business contact channel. Do not collect personal details or invent a direct contact.

Keep three separate fields: business type (retailer, trading company, manufacturer, unknown); verification status (unverified, documents reviewed, independently corroborated); and commercial status (lead, researching, sample requested, sample reviewed, approved, watchlist, rejected, inactive). A store badge, 'factory' in a name or high rating does not establish manufacturing ownership. 'Approved' requires a named reviewer, date, approved scope and supporting evidence, never the research assistant's assumption.

Assess product consistency, sizing documentation, material transparency, communication history, delivery to the target market, return handling, stock reliability, image-use permissions and sample outcomes. Report only evidence-supported concerns, not accusations. Track any claimed certifications with issuing body, certificate number, product scope, date and verification link; leave them unverified if they cannot be independently checked.

Produce a directory-ready record plus a source ledger. List the questions that would resolve meaningful gaps, such as who makes the garment, whether the same chart applies to all variants, how restocks are handled, and which media can be reused. Recommend the next workflow step. Do not send a message, place an order, approve a vendor or publish private documents.

