TASK
Prepare a draft message for the supplier in {{supplier_record}}.
Products and exact variants: {{product_variants}}
Questions from due diligence: {{open_questions}}
Sample budget and quantity: {{sample_budget}}
Target market: {{target_market}}

Write a short, polite, practical message introducing Wow Fashion accurately and requesting the information needed for the proposed relationship. If the project is affiliate-only, do not imply that Wow Fashion is committing to wholesale orders or private labeling. If the operating model is undecided, ask factual questions without making commercial commitments.

Prioritize precise composition, garment measurements and tolerances, size consistency, care instructions, supplier/manufacturer relationship, current availability, shipping estimate to the target destination, returns for sample issues, and permission to reuse product images. Request evidence for claims already made by the supplier; do not demand irrelevant certifications for ordinary clothing.

Create a sample brief with the exact item/variant, quantity, purpose, maximum approved budget, and inspection criteria: received measurements versus chart, label/composition consistency, stitching, fastenings, opacity where relevant, color consistency, and wash checks only where appropriate instructions exist. Separate subjective style preference from observed defects. Record test conditions and limit conclusions to the sampled variant.

Return the ready-to-review message, sample worksheet and fields to update after a reply. Keep placeholders for unknown recipient details. Do not send the message, disclose private information, accept terms or order samples.

