TASK
Write a Wow Fashion roundup about {{topic_and_intent}}.
Approved candidates with current evidence: {{approved_candidates}}
Selection method and scorecards: {{selection_method}}
Physical testing records, if any: {{testing_records}}
Useful existing pages: {{related_urls}}

Start with the reader's decision and present a short comparison table early. Give each item a distinct, supported reason to be included, such as a specific silhouette, verified size range, price position or practical feature. Do not award 'best overall', 'most durable', 'highest quality' or a test-winning label without evidence appropriate to that claim. If research is desk-based, use wording such as 'shortlisted options' and explain the assessment method honestly.

For each product include: suitable use, verified defining features, main limitation, important size/material check, source-check date and retailer link. Keep commentary original and useful rather than rewriting seller descriptions. Distinguish listing-wide review figures from evidence for the selected variant. Include real tradeoffs instead of identical praise for every item. Do not rank by commission rate.

Add a concise 'How we selected these options' section explaining the scope of research, comparison criteria, sampled reviews and whether any hands-on testing occurred. Include buying advice that helps readers choose even if they do not buy a featured product. Cover alternatives if the shortlist has a meaningful gap rather than inventing candidates to meet a list length.

Use approved affiliate disclosures and retailer-specific CTAs where relevant. Prices are time-stamped snapshots for the chosen variant and market, with shipping/tax treatment clear. Return the article, title tag, meta description, internal links and a separate unresolved-facts checklist. Choose length based on useful comparisons, not an arbitrary SEO minimum.

